Interesting tactical innovations:
-- arrive on Medusa level with no obvious means of crossing water.
However,
this is the non-walled variant, and I discover I can cross it -- and
Juiblex level --
using boots of jumping by walking on the provided islands and
carefully choosing my jump
points.

Of course, I  go swimming a few times before getting this down, and
blank all my
scrolls - including the scroll of charging I had wished for at the
castle! Fortunately I find
one in the Valley.

-- When I get to Rodney's house, I wind up killing him over water --
then I can't
find the book! I realize it must have gone into water with him.

After pondering my situation for a bit, I carefully take off all my
armor, put on
a ring of polymorph control, and zap myself with a wand of polymorph.
I turn
into a Xorn, which then goes into the moat and retrieves the undamaged
book!

Once I get back outside, It throw my +5 Grayswandir at the ceiling,
which comes
back down and hits 20hp me, reverting me to my normal human form.


-- identifying gems:  whenever I saw a gem, I would name all gems of
that type as follows: first time I find a soft gem, I name it 'soft
gem 1 occurrence 1". The next time I find a gem of type
'soft gem 1 occurrence 1', I name it 'soft gem 1 occurrence 2' ...
then 3, 4, 5 ... pretty soon I start seeing some types of gems that
are occurring far more often than others, and I rename them 'worthless
glass'.  This worked ... When I ascended I had not made a single
mistake in my inventory. All the gems I thought were valuable were, in
fact, valuable.


--- Did this before, but worth mentioning : I had no magic resistance
for a long time,
so I wore a ring of polymorph control as insurance against polymorph
traps. Ironcially,
I never had to test this.

-- Nasty surprise: While jumping on Juiblex level, try to jump across
water on
top of a potion. This 'potion' turns out to be a mimic, which bounces
me
back into the water. FORTUNATELY, there is other ground nearby.

Another discovery: It APPEARS that luck has an effect on how much of
my
stuff suffers when I go into the water. The first time, I went in and
lost almost everything, with my luck down around 0. When I went in
later with maxed luck, lost almost nothing.

-- YA Nasty surprise: Can't use wand of digging to dig out from
Juiblex level.
When I zap the ground at my feet to evade Juiblex, the pit fills with
water and I
have to scramble to escape. I should have named this guy 'swimmer'.

-- nasty surprise #3: Cursed gold detection does NOT detect traps,
confused
or not confused.  I lose 2 scrolls before discovering I need uncursed
scrolls while
confused to detect traps.  I still have enough to navigate Air and
Earth, but on Fire
I need to fumble around holding the Amulet to find the portal.  Water,
of course,
takes forever to wander around until the amulet finally leads me to
the right portal
and out.

